SYNOPSIS
        mapping update_blueprint_result(int id)

DESCRIPTION
        Read a fresh, non-consuming report for update_blueprint(). Only the
        requesting object or the master may read it. Unknown, cancelled,
        expired, evicted, and unauthorized identifiers raise an error.
        Polling does not execute or advance a request.

        The mapping contains:

          id                    Monotonic request identifier.
          origin                Canonical source load name.
          selection             "all" or "explicit".
          status                "pending" or "failed" in this implementation.
          candidate_generation  Exact candidate's diagnostic generation label.
          matched               Surviving selected clones, including current ones.
          updated               Always zero: migration is not implemented.
          already_current       Clones with the exact candidate program identity.
          destroyed             Destroyed identities from the saved explicit set.
          blueprint_updated     Always zero: migration is not implemented.
          variable_changes      Generation-specific schema and default evidence.
          errors                Terminal reason, compiler diagnostics, and schema blockers.
          completed_at          Completion time in seconds, zero while pending.

        Pending unknowns are zero or empty arrays, including during compiler
        callbacks. Clone counts exclude the blueprint. All-mode discovery
        has no admission snapshot from which to count earlier destruction.
        Strict survivor failures retain the complete discovered counts. If
        the discovery scan itself exceeds its bound, counts remain zero and
        its error explicitly states that selection counts are unavailable.

        Each variable_changes entry identifies old_generation and
        candidate_generation, with matched/added/removed declarations,
        function slot mappings, and concrete compatibility blockers.
        Added declarations contain a "default" decision: literal, implicit,
        shared, or an unsupported/unavailable decision with its reason.
        A shared decision describes copying a blueprint value without
        exposing or retaining that live value. Retained initializers are
        never executed. Literal values are private native preparations.

        Source mode adds one entry for the implicit blueprint generation,
        even without clones. It has "blueprint": 1 and "blueprint_defaults",
        containing added-declaration records with the blueprint's own default
        decisions. The ordinary "added" decisions describe clone defaults
        when that generation has selected clones, otherwise blueprint defaults;
        blueprint_defaults distinguishes literal blueprint preparation from
        clone sharing when both roles have the same old generation. Each
        actual old generation appears only once in the outer array. The
        blueprint_blockers array retains source-default preparation blockers.

        The first error has "code" and "message". Compatible preparation
        ends with IMPLEMENTATION_INCOMPLETE. SCHEMA_INCOMPATIBLE retains
        generation/layout/default blockers in variable_changes and errors.
        Each schema error includes old_generation, candidate_generation, and
        role ("generation" or "blueprint"). Source, target, replacement,
        compilation, and resource failures give their specific reason.
        REPORT_SIZE_LIMIT, COMPILE_DIAGNOSTIC_LIMIT, and
        SCHEMA_DIAGNOSTIC_LIMIT explicitly mean that
        evidence is incomplete; a bounded minimal explanation remains even
        when richer report construction fails. Exceptional allocation or
        callback unwinds may leave only that minimal explanation, including
        REPORT_ALLOCATION_FAILED or PREPARATION_FAILED.

        Compiler rows have code COMPILE_ERROR or COMPILE_WARNING, file, line,
        warning (zero or one), and message. Successful compilation warnings
        are retained too. Collection is bounded to 128 diagnostic rows and
        65536 diagnostic text bytes and shares the request storage allowance.
        Each generation/role retains at most 128 concrete schema blockers;
        overflow adds one SCHEMA_DIAGNOSTIC_LIMIT row and an explicit terminal
        reason while preserving the bounded declaration evidence.
        No terminal report holds source/target objects or program pointers.

        Each read returns independent nested arrays and mappings, preserving
        sharing within the returned value. Mutation or an allocation/evaluation
        failure while copying cannot consume or change the cached report.
        Copying is bounded and obeys the caller's normal array/mapping and
        evaluation limits; it raises instead of returning a partial report.
        Its byte allowance covers the fixed report fields, outer arrays,
        copied values, and conservative native identity-table bookkeeping.

        Terminal reports expire exactly 300 seconds after completion. Reads
        do not renew this time. At most 256 terminal reports are cached;
        eviction removes the oldest completion, breaking equal-time ties by
        the lower ID. This cache is separate from pending-request capacity.
        Requester destruction removes its reports immediately.

SEE ALSO
